## Activity Event table — special note

The activity_event table is NOT dormant — it should be written to in v1 for every meaningful action. What is dormant is the consumption layer: engagement scoring, notification triggers, and org group reporting all read from this table but don't exist yet.

Write to activity_event now for: RSVPs, profile updates, media uploads, invitation sends, join request approvals, payment completions, communication sends.

The schema for activity_event is intentionally generic (actor_id, action_type, object_type, object_id, metadata jsonb) so any future consumer can query it without a migration.

---

## Migration notes for when roadmap features activate

**Engagement scoring:** Add a scheduled Supabase Edge Function that calculates engagement_score on membership records nightly. No schema migration needed.

**Notification triggers:** The notification_trigger table defines rules. A new Edge Function reads activity_event, evaluates rules, and fires notifications. No schema migration needed.

**Vendor marketplace:** Set discoverable = true on vendor_profile records to opt vendors into the directory. Add a public RLS policy for discoverable vendors. No schema migration needed.

**Org group reporting:** Org group records already exist. Aggregate queries run across tenants where org_group_id matches. Add RLS policy for org group admins. No schema migration needed.
